i kept getting questions on how we released clef so quickly after jev, but i strongly believe that we’re mostly reaping the benefits of asymmetric effort: new ideas are difficult to invent and easy to copy.

@typesafeai has done an incredible job in pioneering this concept of system one models. i also strongly believe that it is not a zero-sum game! it’s almost a duty for all of us to solve difficult hardware constraints through software, and system one models allow us to offload some of the work we’d regularly send to LLMs towards smaller, faster, and less compute-intensive models.

